  "goodToKnow": "Der Diener (die Dienerin) is a servant: der Kammerdiener (valet), ein Diener zweier Herren (a servant of two masters, after Goldoni's comedy). Frederick the Great famously called himself der erste Diener des Staates (the first servant of the state). In older German, einen Diener machen meant to bow, as children were taught. From dienen (to serve), related to der Dienst (service)."
